Subject: [PATCH] zune-core: check the ZCursor read end for overflow

`position + N` and `position + buf.len()` overflow when the cursor sits near
usize::MAX. ZSeekFrom::Start puts it wherever the file says, so this is
reachable: in zune-heic, a grid item whose iloc extent offset is
usize::MAX - 1 (0xfffffffe on wasm32) is seeked to, one byte is skipped, and
read_u8_err() then panics on the `get(start..end).unwrap()` in
peek_bytes_impl (release builds; debug builds panic on the addition). The
unit test added here fails without the fix.

Upstream: none found.

diff --git a/crates/zune-core/src/bytestream/reader/no_std_readers.rs b/crates/zune-core/src/bytestream/reader/no_std_readers.rs
index 13670ea..a65eec2 100644
--- a/crates/zune-core/src/bytestream/reader/no_std_readers.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-core/src/bytestream/reader/no_std_readers.rs
